    "1d488 sums cursor and start bytes without byte truncation, then compares against byte end BEFORE calling. Values256..510 skip the callback loop; subsequent indices remain<=the reloaded byte end. Hence each executed table lookup is within entries0..255, assuming ordinary callees preserve local state registers. This does not prove the table contains256 valid functions.",
    "1d7ec, present in the initial second-level tables, writes1 to[P+1] using reloaded global15874; it does not assign global15874. This byte selects an early-return/resumption path in1d488 after callback.",
    "1d714->1f1a4 clearsP+1 then drives1d6f8->1b42c.1d77c->28b50 updates maskP+12 and may drive the same machinery. These handlers do not locally assignP+22c or start/end bytes; their transitive effects remain open.",
    "No fixed-address store to the four initialP+22c cells is located in the retained scan. Same-offset stores with different or unknown bases do not establish either a writer or its absence.",
    "A separate helper1bf68 writes offsets32/33, but its only located caller passes110d4, not one of the four selected structures. Do not infer shared state solely from matching field offsets."
